{"contents":"Hand 20: Loss with 8s Jd from SB. Called S1's raise S5 also called. Flop Kc 3h 4d - bet 12, S1 folded, S5 called. Turn Ks - bet 20, S5 called. River 4c - checked. S5 showed 9d Kd (two pair: kings and fours), won 82. I lost 36 chips: stack 100 now.

Notes: Hand 20/30. 4 active players. I was outdrawn with no pair vs S5's two pair. My betting on flop/turn was aggressive with nothing - should have checked back or folded more often against S5's calling range. S5 is very loose-aggressive with 593 chips (dominant stack). S1 is solid (304). S4 medium (203).

Next hand: BTN=S5, SB=S0(me), BB=S1. I'm in SB again with 100 chips. Tighter play from SB - fold more marginal hands. S5 will be aggressive from BTN position."}

